  "statement": "The office printer firmware only gives you stacks (Python lists with `append` and `pop`), but jobs must print first-in, first-out.\n\nBuild a queue out of **two stacks** and use it to process `ops`, a list of operations:\n\n- `[\"push\", x]` adds `x` to the back (no output)\n- `[\"pop\"]` removes the front value and outputs it\n- `[\"peek\"]` outputs the front value without removing it\n- `[\"empty\"]` outputs `True` if the queue is empty, else `False`\n\nReturn the list of outputs in order. `pop` and `peek` are never called on an empty queue. Do not use `collections.deque` or `list.pop(0)`.",
  "function": {
    "name": "process_queue",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "ops",
        "type": "list[list]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "list"
  },
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= len(ops) <= 10^4",
    "-10^6 <= x <= 10^6"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "args": [
        [
          [
            "push",
            1
          ],
          [
            "push",
            2
          ],
          [
            "peek"
          ],
          [
            "pop"
          ],
          [
            "empty"
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        1,
        1,
        false
      ],
      "explanation": "Front is 1; after popping it, 2 is still queued."
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          [
            "empty"
          ],
          [
            "push",
            5
          ],
          [
            "pop"
          ],
          [
            "empty"
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        true,
        5,
        true
      ],
      "explanation": "The queue starts and ends empty."
    }
  ],
  "starter": {
    "python": "def process_queue(ops):\n    # Write your solution here\n    pass\n"
  },
