  "hints": [
    "A stack reverses order; reversing twice gives the original order back.",
    "Push into an 'in' stack. Serve pop/peek from an 'out' stack.",
    "Only when 'out' is empty, move everything from 'in' to 'out' (pop from one, append to the other). Each value moves at most once, so the cost is O(1) amortised."
  ],
  "followUps": [
    "Can you build a stack using only queue operations?"
  ],
